        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vowinckel_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors the Vowinckel family, early German immigrants who established key lumber operations in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/vowinckel_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Vowinckel sits on the Allegheny Plateau at 1,637 feet, overlooking the Clarion River valley and surrounded by oak, maple, and hemlock forests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
